   "evidence": "Theorem `one_sub_norm_charFun_spatialPart_sub_le` (Coherence.lean:89) bounds `1 - \u2016charFun \u03bc (p - p').spatialPart\u2016` by `-\u27eaq,q\u27eb\u2098 * (1 + -\u27eaq,q\u27eb\u2098 / (4 * m ^ 2)) * (\u222b r, \u2016r\u2016 ^ 2 \u2202\u03bc) / 2`; the factor `(1 + Q\u00b2/(4m\u00b2))` is unbounded as `m \u2192 0` at fixed `Q\u00b2`.",
   "file": "EpsilonEridani/QFT/Scattering/Photoproduction/Coherence.lean",
   "fix": "State the extra condition, e.g. \"\u2026 while `Q\u00b2 R\u00b2` is small against one and the recoil factor `Q\u00b2/(4m\u00b2)` is bounded, which `Q\u00b2 R\u00b2 \u2272 1` gives for a source with `m R \u2273 1`\".",
   "issue": "The module docstring concludes \"So `\u2016F\u2016` stays close to one, the value for a point charge, while `Q\u00b2 R\u00b2` is small against one\" from the bound `1 - \u2016F(q)\u2016 \u2264 Q\u00b2 (1 + Q\u00b2 / (4 m\u00b2)) R\u00b2 / 2`. The conclusion does not follow from that bound alone: the recoil factor makes the right-hand side `Q\u00b2R\u00b2/2 + Q\u2074R\u00b2/(8m\u00b2)`, which with only `Q\u00b2R\u00b2 \u2264 1` is bounded by `(1 + 1/(4m\u00b2R\u00b2))/2` and is not small when `m R \u226a 1`.",
   "line": 34
  }
